course: dictionary
lesson: 4159
title: Words with a silent letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gnome is a tiny old man from fairy tales who lives under the ground and guards treasure. Today, a garden gnome is often a small painted statue with a pointed hat, put in a garden for fun.
explain: Use the words around a word to find its meaning. «Leo broke the garden gnome with his bat and buried the pieces with his friend, laughing.» The words garden and buried tell you the gnome is an object in a garden, not a real man.
explain: Gnome has a silent g. You do not say the g, so the word sounds like "nome". It belongs to the gn group, which you will also see in gnaw and gnat.
fact: A gnome is a tiny old man in fairy tales who lives under the ground and guards treasure.
fact: A garden gnome is a small painted statue of a bearded little man with a pointed hat.
fact: Informally, a gnome can mean a small, odd-looking person, and this can be unkind.
fact: The g in gnome is silent, so you say "nome". Other silent-letter groups include kn (knife, knee) and wr (write, wrong).
fact: «The gnomes of Zurich» is an old joke name for Swiss bankers.
exercise: «Leo broke the garden gnome with his bat and buried the pieces with his friend, laughing.» What is a garden gnome? | A small boat on a lake | A large tree in a park | A kind of wet weather | *A small painted statue for a garden
exercise: In a fairy tale, what does a gnome live under and guard? | Old bicycles | Sheep | *Treasure | Ice cream
exercise: Which letter is silent in gnome? | The o | The e | *The first g | The m
test: Which word has a silent letter like gnome? | Garden | Happy | *Knee | Table
test: In slang, what can gnome mean? | A long road | A bright star | *A small, odd-looking person | A big, loud dog
exam: Sam says the g in gnome is said out loud. What is the correct answer? | Yes, the g is said clearly, like in go | Yes, it sounds like gnu, with a hard g | *No, the g is silent, so the word sounds like nome | No, the g is said but the n is silent
